# Esper Origins, cast from the hand and then with flashback from the graveyard ({3}{G}). Both casts surveil 2 and gain 2
# life. Only the flashback cast was "cast from a graveyard": that one exiles itself (CR 608.2m) and puts the card onto the
# battlefield transformed (CR 712.14a) under its owner's control with a finality counter on it. It enters as Summon: Esper
# Maduin, a green (its color indicator) 4/4 Enchantment Creature - Saga Elemental, with the finality counter and the lore
# counter a Saga enters with (CR 714.3a) both on it as it enters (CR 122.6, 614.1c). The lore counter triggers chapter I
# (CR 714.2b): the top card, Llanowar Elves (left there by the second surveil), is revealed and, a permanent card, put
# into Bot1's hand. Nothing is left in exile: the card that was exiled is the permanent now.

